WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.706
Grid: draw the tracks first, then let the items fall into place.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.194
Here is an empty box, 920px wide. We make it a grid.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:19.194
Three columns: 200px, 1fr, 2fr. Nothing is inside yet, but the columns already exist.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.725
Between them run numbered lines. Three columns have four lines, 1 to 4.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.836
How wide is 1fr? The browser works it out last.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:37.034
Start with 920. Subtract the fixed track, 200. Subtract 2 gaps of 10.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:46.027
700px are free. They are shared in three parts: 1fr is about 233px, 2fr about 467px.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:51.396
Resize the box and the fixed track stays put. Only the fr tracks stretch.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.096
Now the items arrive. You don't say where they go.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.630
Auto-placement fills the cells in HTML order, left to right.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.818
When a row is full, a new row starts. That's why you usually define only the columns.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.906
repeat(3, 1fr) is short for 1fr 1fr 1fr.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:22.772
minmax(200px, 1fr): never narrower than 200px, growing to fill the row.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.815
Add auto-fit, and the grid adds or drops columns as the box changes. No media query.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.488
You can also place an item yourself, using those line numbers.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:44.371
grid-column: 1 / 3 runs from line 1 to line 3. That covers 2 columns, not 3.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:50.244
span 2 says the same without counting. 1 / -1 means the full width.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.083
The other items auto-place around it. No extra HTML.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:04.839
For a whole page, name the regions. Each quoted string is one row; each word is one cell.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:12.583
Header, twice. Sidebar and content. Footer, twice. A name repeated across cells spans them.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:19.252
Each element claims its region with grid-area. One without it falls into a free cell, in the wrong place.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:26.888
On a phone, redraw the strings as one column. The sidebar drops below the content, and the HTML never changes.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.514
So Flexbox or Grid? Look at the shape of the problem.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.667
A nav is one line of items, sized by their content. Flexbox.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.976
A page has rows and columns that must line up. The layout decides the sizes. Grid.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:51.398
Most pages use both: a grid for the skeleton, flex rows inside the regions.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.809
Practise it with the Grid playground in CSS.
